{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model underpredicts realized prices across most horizons (typ. ~+2 to +8 EUR/t needed), especially during strong uptrends.",
    "Trend/lag error: model reacts too slowly to regime shifts upward; apply a momentum/trend uplift when last 5–10 days show sustained gains (e.g., add extra +1 to +3 EUR/t on top of baseline bias in rising regimes).",
    "Horizon-dependent underestimation: the underprediction is larger in the mid-horizon (~day 5–20) than at day 1–3; use an increasing bias adjustment into the mid-horizon, then taper.",
    "Over-mean-reversion in forecasts: model pulls prices back toward ~72–76 even when realized stays elevated (~80–84); reduce mean-reversion strength when spot is breaking to new 30-day highs.",
    "Late-horizon downside overshoot: when the model projects a decline in days ~25–30, it often falls too far/too early versus realized; dampen negative slopes in the tail (shrink projected drawdowns).",
    "After spike behavior: model tends to fade rallies too quickly; following sharp up-moves, cap any forecasted retracement over the next 1–2 weeks unless recent realized prices have already started to roll over."
  ]
}
